# BearSSL against OpenSSL on AES-GCM (spec section 8.2), on native, wasip2 and
# wasip3. The portable twin keeps BearSSL on aes_ct64 and ghash_ctmul64
# through the backend's test seam, so that on x86-64 both of BearSSL's code
# paths are compared with OpenSSL's. On WASI OpenSSL runs its portable C code
# (no-asm, tools/openssl/build.py), another pair of implementations.
